    "description": "A bath complex of ancient Rome built on the Aventine Hill in 252 CE.",
    "details": "<p>Some elements of the bath complex were still visible in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries, as architect Andrea Palladio produced a plan of the central bath block around 1600. Rodolfo Lanciani later rediscovered this Palladian plan. Thepresent-day churches of S. Alessio and S. Prisca occupy the area of the bath complex. The casino of the Vigna Torlonia reuses some of the ancient foundations.</p>",
